    Assemble the production proximity plan and carry the session in the proof package
    
    The trusted planner now assembles the production proximity configuration from the reference production policy mapped to the one-main-code layout this executor supports: a bounded candidate choice, the first-stage fold bits from the real member rows, the stage-0 main and mask tails from the joint solve including the SEND and shared reads, each later stage's positions solved from its own rounds, and the exact frozen round count as the reserved budget. A planner-checked plan is re-derived on the verifier side from the same trusted shapes and public choices: a changed position, tail, code, BASE count or fold bit is rejected, and no configuration is searched for on the verifier.
    
    The projection consumer's hidden session now uses the assembled codes and stage lists with the planner check on. The canonical session encoding enters the verification package as session.bin next to the trusted commitment and the trace; the verifier decodes it from the package and checks the proof again from those bytes alone.
    
    Evidence: the workspace is green (1014 passed, 0 failed, 19 ignored); the norm-free toy output-head proof is unchanged at 45,080 bytes with digest 7a5da6ebcbfdb61d5ee88ab60e67f45613906959b0c5de998cb870f5e1de4cfb; the real registered seq16 consumer run proves and verifies with the assembled plan in 78.33 s and a 1,075,512-byte session.
    
    The closure and norm members of the planner-checked assembly are the next step.

